 "text": "Reading about your goal feels like doing it, it isn't. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 24. Say you want to write a book, three books on writing, 40 videos. Pages written zero but it feels like weeks of work. Learning feels like progress, you're busy and it's all about the goal but nothing gets made. Then one day you see how far you haven't come, you quit. So flip the order, make first, learn second. Write a hundred words then watch one video, run 50 minutes then read about form. Six weeks later, 4000 words not 40 videos. Send this to the friend with a full bookmarks folder and an empty page. That's what Demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why you stop improving after month one. What are you reading about instead of doing, the links in the bio.",
